STEP 0: CREATE REPOSITORY ON GITHUB
Repository name: lab
Select Public → Create repository

STEP 1: CLONE
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/lab.git
cd lab

STEP 2: CREATE FILE
echo "Hello, GitHub" > file1.txt
cat file1.txt

STEP 3: COMMIT AND PUSH
git add file1.txt
git commit -m "Initial"
git push -u origin main

STEP 4: CREATE BRANCH
git branch feature1
git checkout feature1

STEP 5: MODIFY FEATURE BRANCH
notepad file1.txt

Add: Feature branch update

git add file1.txt
git commit -m "Feature branch update"
git push -u origin feature1

STEP 6: COMPARE
git diff main feature1

STEP 7: CREATE MERGE CONFLICT
git checkout main
notepad file1.txt

Replace contents with:
Hello, GitHub
Main branch change

git add file1.txt
git commit -m "Main branch change"
git merge feature1

STEP 8: RESOLVE CONFLICT
notepad file1.txt

Remove conflict markers and replace contents with:
Hello, GitHub
Main branch change
Feature branch update

git add file1.txt
git commit -m "Merge conflict resolved"
git push origin main

STEP 9: PREPARE PULL REQUEST
git checkout feature1
notepad file1.txt

Add: Pull request

git add file1.txt
git commit -m "Prepare pull request"
git push origin feature1

STEP 10: CREATE PULL REQUEST
GitHub → lab → Pull requests → New pull request
Base: main
Compare: feature1
Create pull request
Resolve conflicts if prompted
Commit resolution if prompted
Merge pull request → Confirm

FINAL VERIFICATION
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git status
cat file1.txt
